{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01292",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.53,
      "end_seconds": 5.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I came as soon as they called me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.68,
      "end_seconds": 10.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.68,
      "end_seconds": 15.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "I've been feeling dizzy when I stand up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.1,
      "end_seconds": 18.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.03,
      "end_seconds": 31.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.34,
      "end_seconds": 50.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.51,
      "text": "Okay: temp 36.7 degrees, saturation 97 percent. And pulse 100, BP is 104 over 64."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.18,
      "end_seconds": 70.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "So, did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.59,
      "end_seconds": 78.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Right, for five days, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.0,
      "end_seconds": 88.09,
      "duration_seconds": 8.09,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.47,
      "end_seconds": 107.37,
      "duration_seconds": 17.9,
      "text": "Getting out of bed and standing up quickly definitely sets it off. Maybe a five out of ten on a bad day. Oh, and a dry mouth. That's been about the same, about four days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.19,
      "end_seconds": 113.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.11,
      "end_seconds": 118.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "I'd call it severe. Sipping water helps a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.14,
      "end_seconds": 137.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Have you noticed slurred speech, fainting or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.58,
      "end_seconds": 142.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.19,
      "end_seconds": 146.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Any black stools or chest pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.05,
      "end_seconds": 154.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "No, no black stools or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.44,
      "end_seconds": 157.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.64,
      "end_seconds": 163.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.03,
      "end_seconds": 169.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.82,
      "end_seconds": 173.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.42,
      "end_seconds": 177.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.48,
      "end_seconds": 187.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for about a year. I have heart failure, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.86,
      "end_seconds": 195.79,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "Alright, heart failure, that matches what I have here. Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.9,
      "end_seconds": 200.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "No, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.95,
      "end_seconds": 205.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.61,
      "end_seconds": 217.71,
      "duration_seconds": 7.1,
      "text": "Telmisartan. I take it 40 milligrams, once a day. Carvedilol, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.55,
      "end_seconds": 220.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.1,
      "end_seconds": 232.2,
      "duration_seconds": 10.1,
      "text": "6.25 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box. I used to take amlodipine, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.8,
      "end_seconds": 235.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.47,
      "end_seconds": 240.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.22,
      "end_seconds": 244.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Okay, anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.14,
      "end_seconds": 249.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.22,
      "end_seconds": 253.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.3,
      "end_seconds": 258.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.46,
      "end_seconds": 264.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.49,
      "end_seconds": 267.43,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.44,
      "end_seconds": 270.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.01,
      "end_seconds": 292.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal and the chest is clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.51,
      "end_seconds": 296.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.03,
      "end_seconds": 324.31,
      "duration_seconds": 18.28,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, I'd lean towards postural low blood pressure, possibly related to medicines or dehydration. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I can't rule out dehydration yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.18,
      "end_seconds": 330.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.93,
      "end_seconds": 352.25,
      "duration_seconds": 20.32,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like postural low blood pressure, possibly related to medicines or dehydration, but I'd like to confirm. Let's book blood tests to look into dizziness. Get up slowly from lying and sitting, and keep drinking fluids through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.46,
      "end_seconds": 376.43,
      "duration_seconds": 23.97,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. A lying and standing blood pressure check is something we might do if this doesn't improve in two weeks. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 377.15,
      "end_seconds": 381.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}